motivation: You do not have to be ready. You have to be present, then begin.
discipline: Discipline is just love for tomorrow's you. It shows up in the small, unglamorous minutes.
money: Let your savings wait, your spending serve a purpose, and your possessions answer to you.
mindset: Fear can sit beside me without holding the pen. I still write the next line.
fact: Your stomach lining replaces itself every few days, otherwise it would digest itself.
books: A growth mindset turns failure into information, not a verdict on your fixed worth.
stoic: We keep postponing life, as if it will wait until we are ready.
